## Historical Notification Page Checkpoint

The notification page now uses the Base detail composition. Earlier source
checkpoints below are historical, not runtime release evidence.

- Task source: `29c405f084058965a6f8894cacd2362b2d8fa791`.
- Base source: `26a9523bf739c2fb4aafa343fdbc194d02a78e6a`.
- Base installed/source fingerprint:
  `3af92a8c2fba948b7967ebc8338fb0c27c8a08e702af0351b8c390910bb93d11`.
- Product fingerprint:
  `8b977864dcf3ac63334791bc9eaca641aeb76f7e5f269cc7fc46f4eb90de3500`.
- Frozen offline force install reused all 503 packages without lockfile or
  generated API schema drift. Public APIs and database schemas did not change.

| Command | Exit | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile --force` | 0 | `task-notification-page-install.log` |
| `pnpm test` | 0 | `task-notification-page-units.log`; 371 tests, 47 files |
| `pnpm lint` | 0 | `task-notification-page-lint.log`; ESLint and semantic classes |
| `pnpm build` | 0 | `task-notification-page-build.log`; typecheck and Vite |
| `pnpm ui:check -- --fingerprint` | 0 | `task-notification-page-ui-gate.log`; 16 route patterns |
| Chromium smoke, one worker, `--max-failures=1` | 0 | `task-notification-page-final-browser.log`; 10 tests, 5.1 minutes |
| README validator and Python script tests | 0 | README validation and 4 script tests |
| Scoped Prettier and `git diff --check` | 0 | reviewed source delta |

- `/notifications` declares `detail-with-aside` in the shell and route manifest.
  DetailPage owns the sole page heading and the 320 px aside/1024 breakpoint.
  Local Card wrappers, the 304 px grid and bespoke filter buttons were removed.
- List and preferences use independent Base resource states. Unknown unread
  counts are not zero. Cached 403/404 hide the affected source and unsafe actions;
  retryable refresh preserves readonly content/drafts, without disabling an
  unrelated healthy source. Feedback is localized and does not expose envelopes.
- Base Tabs/codecs preserve unrelated query/hash, direct/reload and Back/Forward.
  Filters reset pagination; empty pages reset only on successful reads. Page bounds
  protect integer offset precision without imposing a new backend limit.
- PendingForm/FormField/Select, draft guard and ConfirmDialog own common behavior.
  Refetch and query navigation preserve edited preferences and unknown event types.
  Failed saves retain input. Pending prevents double submissions; discard requires
  confirmation and restores focus. Revoked settings hide, but do not discard, drafts.
- One/all marking is synchronously locked; failed mark-all retains pagination,
  success resets it, and completion cannot navigate back from an unmounted page.
  Only repeatable write failures offer retry after the list source is healthy.
  Removed rows restore safe focus without stealing an intentional focus move.
  A link blocked by an unsaved-preferences guard does not prematurely mark read.
- Browser testing exposed duplicate history entries from pointer selection plus
  default focus on controlled Tabs. Base now suppresses the duplicate callback
  through the gesture, retaining keyboard/uncontrolled behavior and later retries.
  `base-tabs-history-units.log`: 99 UI tests (23 files), 18 script tests and contrast;
  Base lint/typecheck and README/hub validators passed. The microtask-only
  intermediate fix was insufficient and is superseded by the final snapshot.
- Final output contains 222 PNG: the earlier 188 captures on current source,
  30 notification page captures (three themes, ten widths) and four controlled
  page states. Actual geometry, 40/44 targets, local/document overflow, URL history,
  pending/draft/focus scenarios passed. Axe found no main-scope violations for
  this page at 375/1920 in three themes; normal page console/network checks passed.
  Representative desktop/mobile/breakpoint and controlled-state images were viewed.

Artifacts: [final captures](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-notification-page-final-browser/),
[browser log](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-notification-page-final-browser.log).
Earlier focused/history diagnostic runs are superseded, including the reproduced
duplicate-history failure; they are not green acceptance evidence.

HTTP/OIDC is mocked. The owned preview terminated and port 18865 has no listener.
No runtime pins/images, secrets/volumes, foreign checkouts, default refs or mirror
were changed. All original findings remain open pending full release evidence.
Legacy header-counter typography/theme CSS, remaining route compositions and
states, full backend gates, no-mock actual images/live SSO/roles, real README
provenance, synchronized consumers, local integration and mirror remain required.

